{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: Durable Object row-write accounting and a billing gate before the durable deployment (hugh, 2026-10-02; lessons from woo in the planner's assert on write storms; simplification review 55563589). (1) Measure, from Cloudflare's Durable Object billing datasets and not from application counters, the physical rows written by the spike deployment for: one claim, one propose, one review, one check, one land, one note, one join; one alarm tick with nothing pending; one alarm tick with one pending pin; one publication; one policy activation with N open proposals; one landing with N open previews; founding one room; and the same for rows read. Record the table and the method in packages/room/measure/results and a dated section of notes/deploy-spike.md, with the index count per table from room/src/store.ts explaining the multiplier. (2) Port the approach of woo's scripts/cloudflare-do-storage.ts and net-storage-gate.ts (at ~/play/woo, commits 6d2c425a and 50163fc1): attribute rows written per namespace and per object over a recorded window, fail closed on missing token, missing namespace, absent invocation evidence or truncation, and enforce a total and a per-object budget. Wire it into spike-smoke.mjs as an acceptance gate with initial ceilings grounded by a clean run, and as a scheduled check that can alert. (3) From the measurements, set the budgets the other cost requests cite: the attention fan-out cap per item, the idem and attention FIFO quotas, and the alarm rate. Do not deploy production Workers; the spike names and namespaces only; no credential creation beyond a read-only analytics token, which hugh creates. This precedes J2 in the self-hosting tracker 7a3bbf8f.","body":{"conditions":"A measured table of physical rows written and read per operation from the billing API, with the window and namespace IDs recorded; a fail-closed rows-written gate in the spike smoke run with recorded ceilings; a scheduled check; budgets proposed for attention fan-out, idem and attention retention and alarm rate, filed against 99782949; checker review.","target_head":"a6330262b1a609843308d9a493dbd6132d428499","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}